 ## Human-readable summary
 
 This PR is a preparation layer only. It creates tested, isolated logic for trip-summary rows and future override storage. It does not alter the live app, does not write to the user's real localStorage or Firestore, and does not change deployment behavior.
+
+---
+
+## PR #126 — Trip summary overrides cloud sync
+
+Date: 2026-08-15
+Branch: `feature/trip-summary-cloud-sync`
+Backup branch: `backup/pre-trip-summary-cloud-sync-2026-08-15`
+
+### Purpose
+
+Persist the manual trip-summary corrections added in PR #125 to Firestore, while keeping them isolated from all existing app data.
+
+### Files changed
+
+- `app.html`
+- `docs/CLAUDE_TRIP_SUMMARY_CHANGELOG.md`
+
+### App changes in `app.html`
+
+The cloud sync is intentionally scoped to one new Firestore document:
+
+- Firestore collection/doc: `appdata/trip_summary`
+
+The existing local override keys remain the local source/cache:
+
+- `prague_trip_summary_overrides_v1`
+- `prague_trip_summary_overrides_ts`
+
+Added functions:
+
+- `_tripSummaryOverridesLocalTs()`
+- `_tripSummaryOverridesMeaningful(o)`
+- `_saveTripSummaryOverridesToCloud(o, ts)`
+- `_applyTripSummaryOverridesFromCloud(d)`
+- `initTripSummaryOverridesCloudSync()`
+
+Integration points:
+
+- `_saveTripSummaryOverrides(o)` now writes local first and then attempts isolated Firestore save.
+- `_resyncLocalDataToCloud()` now uploads local trip-summary overrides after login only if local override data exists.
+- `_showApp()` starts the isolated trip-summary listener when the authenticated app is displayed.
+- `BUILD_ID` is updated to `2026-08-15-c`.
+
+### Safety boundaries
+
+This PR must not touch or reuse:
+
+- `appdata/main`
+- `appdata/expenses`
+- `prague_days_v1`
+- `prague_visited_v1`
+- `prague_exp_v10`
+- GAS / backend login code
+
+Conflict protection:
+
+- Empty remote trip-summary state does not overwrite meaningful local override data.
+- Older remote timestamp does not overwrite newer local override data; local newer data is pushed back to `appdata/trip_summary`.
+- Firestore save uses `{ merge: true }` on the isolated document.
